  "step_2": "The individual reports: 'I wanted to rely on my luck and hoped that the 50/50 chance represented a good opportunity, possibly ending up with no losses. Whether I end up losing 500 or 1000 euros doesn't make a big difference to me anyway.' The individual explicitly considers the 50% chance of avoiding a loss (i.e., getting 0€) in Lottery A and views this as a 'good opportunity' due to luck. The justification centers on the possibility of avoiding any loss entirely, which is only possible in Lottery A. The individual downplays the difference between losing 500€ and 1000€, indicating that the magnitude of loss beyond the possibility of zero loss is not a key concern. Thus, the focus is on the chance of the best possible outcome (0€) and the role of luck, rather than on full distributional shape or skewness per se.",
